  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe import of `twisted_flank_off.step` is refused at `crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step/record.rs:158-169`. The refusal names solid `#117`, the 0.343 mm gap and the 1e-3 mm limit. It does not name the edge or the vertex.\n\nThis came with the solidcore bump of PR #3802 (head `c2399c040`). The old kernel named the face.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe user cannot see which part of the model is wrong. The information is in the candidate: `body.worst_edge` holds the kernel edge and the vertex point.\n\n`check_source_topology` at `crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step/record.rs:94-101` already writes the same value as \"Input-record edge index N, vertex (x, y, z) mm\".\n\n## Fix\n\nMap `body.worst_edge` to the input-record edge, and to the face when the record has it, in the refusal at `record.rs:158-169`. Use the same form as lines 94-101.\n\nThen `crates/app/tests/import_step_twisted_flank.rs` can pin the face or the edge again.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe file is still refused. The toolpath output is not wrong. The defect is a missing detail in the refusal text.\n",
